---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro'

// https://docs.astro.build/en/recipes/dynamically-importing-paintings/
const images = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>('../assets/hanging-planters/*.jpg')
---

<PageLayout title="DIY hanging planter tutorial">

  <div class="plantersPage">

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='All the supplies required for the project'
          class="stepImage"
          priority
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/supplies.jpg']() }
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong>Supplies</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Here are the supplies and tools you'll need for this project. The cost
          of materials listed here comes to about $50–60 but you'll have enough
          for multiple planters.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          For craft hoops you'll need one that's smaller than the bottom of the
          pot and one that's large enough to accommodate both the pot and foliage.
          I used 2–3″ for the smaller ones and anywhere from 7–12″ for the larger
          rings.
        </p>
        <p class:list={ ["supplies", "paragraph"] }>
          <a class='link' href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B07ND4CNYX">Craft hoops</a>
          <a class='link' href="https://www.amazon.com/Tenn-Well-Industrial-Decoration-Gardening/dp/B01M0TT9YS">Jute twine</a>
          <a class='link' href="https://www.amazon.com/Dritz-PRY-653111-653111-Liquid-Multicolor/dp/B0018NA0F8">Liquid Stitch</a>
          <a class='link' href="https://www.amazon.com/Artistic-34-Gauge-Non-Tarnish-Brass-30-Yards/dp/B004CYFFIC">34-gauge wire</a>
          <a class='link' href="https://www.amazon.com/Artistic-20-Gauge-Non-Tarnish-Brass-15-Yards/dp/B000ONF116">20-gauge wire</a>
          <a class='link' href="https://www.amazon.com/Wento-Brushed-Carabiner-Trigger-Keyring/dp/B07544P8YH">Round carabiners (2 per planter)</a>
          <a class='link' href="https://www.amazon.com/Beadsmith-Variety-Plated-Crimp-Beads/dp/B007JMCD6Q">Crimp tube beads</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='The craft hoop, covered in twine'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/01.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong class="stepNumber">Step 1:</strong>
        <strong>Cover the small craft hoop in jute twine</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Wrap twine tightly around the smaller craft hoop, then secure the ends
          with Liquid Stitch. Your wrapped hoop should rest flat on the bottom of
          your pot.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='The craft hoop, with four marker lines at the cardinal directions'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/02.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong class="stepNumber">Step 2:</strong>
        <strong>Mark where your wires will go</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Using a pen or thin Sharpie, mark 4 points equidistant from each other on
          the circle.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Graph paper makes this easy. Rest your hoop so that each edge is equidistant
          from where two lines cross (in my example, the edges are each four boxes
          away from where the two darker lines meet). Then make a small line where
          each arm of the + crosses the hoop.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='Measure the wire by putting it inside the hoop'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/03.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong class="stepNumber">Step 3:</strong>
        <strong>Calculate how much wire you'll need</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Loop the 34-gauge wire around the hoop. Place your pot (preferably with the
          plant inside) on the hoop. Put this near the edge of a table.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Hold the larger hoop around your pot as you'd like it to hang when the
          planter is finished. Pull the loose end of the wire up until it touches the
          large loop, then pull it an extra 3 inches or so.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Bring the spool of wire up to meet the loose end so that the wire is doubled
          up. Then cut the wire off the spool.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='Close-up of the wire looped around the hoop'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/04.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong class="stepNumber">Step 4:</strong>
        <strong>Cut the rest of your hanging wires</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Use the wire from Step 3 to measure and cut three more pieces of wire.
          Then loop each wire around the small hoop at the marks you made in Step 2.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='A complete hanging loop'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/05.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong class="stepNumber" >Step 5:</strong>
        <strong>Create one hanging loop</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Thread a crimp bead on each set of wires. Rest your pot on the small hoop
          near the edge of a table. Hold the larger hoop around your pot like you
          did in Step 3.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Pull the loose ends of the wire up and bend them gently around the large
          hoop where your fingers are holding it.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Feed the ends of the wires back down through the crimp bead, then guide
          them up and back down through the crimp bead. Tug to tighten and then
          crimp with pliers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='A larger hanging loop'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/06.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong class="stepNumber">Step 6:</strong>
        <strong>Create the rest of your hanging loops</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Measure the total length of the wire from Step 6, from hoop to the
          top of the loop. If the finished wires aren't all the same length,
          your pot won't hang straight!
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Repeat the process from Step 6 to create loops on the remaining
          three sets of wires.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='The loop of wire hanging from a circular carabiner'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/07.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong class="stepNumber">Step 7:</strong>
        <strong>Thread each loop through the carabiner</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Pretty easy!
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='The large hoop on the carabiner also, with a plant inside'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/08.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong class="stepNumber">Step 8:</strong>
        <strong>Put the larger hoop on the carabiner</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          This is also pretty easy 😄
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='Hanging the carabiner from a curtain rod'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/09.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong class="stepNumber">Step 9:</strong>
        <strong>Wire it up</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Run a wire in the desired length from your carabiner up to your
          hanging carabiner. Make a loop on each end for easy removal.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          You can also clip one plant on to the larger craft hoop of another
          plant hanger. Just be conscious of the weight limit of the
          carabiners you're using.
        </p>
        <p class="paragraph">
          I hang my plants from a 2″ curtain rod because I like how it looks.
          The opening of the carabiner isn't big enough for me to clip/unclip
          them from the rod, but if I want to rearrange the plants to
          accommodate new additions it's fairly easy for me to unclip the
          plant from the carabiner and move it to another clip.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <div class="stepImageContainer">
        <Image
          alt='The finished project'
          src={ images['../assets/hanging-planters/done.jpg']() }
          class="stepImage"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="stepText">
        <strong>All done 🌱🌿🌻</strong>
        <p class="paragraph">
          Now you can sit back, relax and enjoy your plants!
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .plantersPage {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 25px 50px 25px;
    max-width: 800px;
    padding-top: var(--page-top-padding);
  }

  .supplies {
    align-items: flex-start;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .supplies :global(.link) {
    margin: 2px 0;
  }

  .step {
    align-items: flex-start;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }

  .stepImageContainer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    margin: 0 0 20px 0;
    height: 250px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .stepImage {
    height: 100%;
    width: auto;
  }

  .stepText {
    border-left: none;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    padding-left: 0;
  }

  .stepNumber {
    margin-right: 4px;
  }


  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .plantersPage {
      margin: 0 auto 50px auto;
      max-width: 800px;
    }

    .step {
      flex-direction: row;
      justify-content: flex-end;
    }

    .stepImageContainer {
      justify-content: flex-end;
      margin: 0 20px 0 0;
    }

    .stepText {
      border-left: 1px dotted #999;
      padding-left: 15px;
      width: 450px;
    }

    .paragraph:last-of-type {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
